<h2>Live data sources</h2>
<p>Loaded live from each source's own server, not stored in this project.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://explorer.adaptingtorisingtides.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BCDC Bay Shoreline Flood Explorer</a> — CC-BY-SA (via the Caltrans open data portal). Attribute Caltrans/BCDC; redistributed copies of the dataset must stay share-alike. Planning-level only — see <a href="https://explorer.adaptingtorisingtides.org/about/a-disclaimer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BCDC's disclaimer</a>.</li>
<li><a href="https://eccexplorer.adaptingtorisingtides.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BCDC East Contra Costa Shoreline Flood Explorer</a> — same program, server, and terms as the Bay explorer above: CC-BY-SA (via the Caltrans open data portal); attribute Caltrans/BCDC. Planning-level only — see <a href="https://eccexplorer.adaptingtorisingtides.org/about/a-disclaimer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BCDC's disclaimer</a>.</li>
<li><a href="https://cmip5.cal-adapt.org/tools/slr-coastal-inundation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cal-Adapt Sea Level Rise – Coastal Inundation Scenarios</a> — CoSMoS (USGS, U.S. public domain) and CalFloD3D-TFS (California Energy Commission / California's Fourth Climate Change Assessment) flood extents, mosaicked and served by Cal-Adapt (UC Berkeley Geospatial Innovation Facility). The tool page states no separate license; attribute Cal-Adapt and cite the studies behind each model:
<ul>
<li>CoSMoS: Barnard, P.L., Erikson, L.H., Foxgrover, A.C., Finzi Hart, J.A., Limber, P., O'Neill, A.C., van Ormondt, M., Vitousek, S., Wood, N., Hayden, M.K., &amp; Jones, J.M. (2019). Dynamic flood modeling essential to assess the coastal impacts of climate change. <em>Scientific Reports</em>, 9, Article 4309. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-40742-z" target="_blank" rel="noopener">doi:10.1038/s41598-019-40742-z</a></li>
<li>CalFloD3D-TFS: Radke, J., et al. (2018). <em>Assessing extreme weather-related vulnerability and identifying resilience options for California's interdependent transportation fuel sector.</em> California's Fourth Climate Change Assessment, California Energy Commission, CCCA4-CEC-2018-012. <a href="https://www.energy.ca.gov/sites/default/files/2019-11/Energy_CCCA4-CEC-2018-012_ADA.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PDF</a></li>
</ul></li>
<li><a href="https://www.usgs.gov/centers/pcmsc/science/coastal-storm-modeling-system-cosmos" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USGS CoSMoS / Our Coast, Our Future</a> — U.S. public domain. Served via Point Blue Conservation Science.</li>
<li><a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/slr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA Sea Level Rise Viewer</a> — U.S. public domain.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.fema.gov/flood-maps/national-flood-hazard-layer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FEMA National Flood Hazard Layer</a> — U.S. public domain.</li>
<li><a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/digitalcoast/tools/flood-exposure.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA Coastal Flood Exposure Mapper</a> — U.S. public domain.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/nationalsurge/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA/NWS/NHC National Storm Surge Risk Maps</a> — U.S. public domain.</li>
<li>Geo / demographic info layers, each loaded from the agency that publishes the data: <a href="https://www.epa.gov/smartgrowth/smart-location-mapping" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EPA Smart Location Database</a> (population and jobs density) and <a href="https://www.epa.gov/frs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EPA Facility Registry Service</a>; <a href="https://www.atsdr.cdc.gov/place-health/php/svi/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CDC/ATSDR Social Vulnerability Index</a> (poverty, age 65+); <a href="https://www.usgs.gov/national-digital-trends/structures" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USGS The National Map Structures</a> (critical facilities); <a href="https://coast.noaa.gov/digitalcoast/data/ccapregional.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA C-CAP land cover and Wetland Potential</a> — all U.S. public domain. <a href="https://data.ca.gov/dataset/annual-average-daily-traffic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Caltrans traffic volumes</a> and <a href="https://data.ca.gov/dataset/truck-average-daily-traffic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">truck volumes</a> — CC BY (attribute Caltrans).</li>
<li><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a> — ODbL. Base map data (all basemaps).</li>
<li><a href="https://openfreemap.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenFreeMap</a> and <a href="https://openmaptiles.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenMapTiles</a> — free, keyless hosting of the default greyscale (Positron) vector basemap; style and code MIT, schema/design CC-BY 4.0.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.hotosm.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Humanitarian OpenStreetMap Team</a> style, hosted by <a href="https://openstreetmap.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap France</a> — optional Humanitarian basemap (light use).</li>
<li><a href="https://www.esri.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Esri World Imagery</a> — optional Satellite basemap, for visualization only, with Esri/Maxar attribution.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/domoritz/leaflet-locatecontrol" target="_blank" rel="noopener">leaflet.locatecontrol</a> (MIT) — the "show my location" button; loaded from unpkg with SRI hashes.</li>
<li><a href="https://maplibre.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MapLibre GL JS</a> (BSD-3-Clause) and <a href="https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-leaflet" target="_blank" rel="noopener">maplibre-gl-leaflet</a> (ISC) — render the vector basemap; loaded from unpkg with SRI hashes.</li>
<li><a href="https://nominatim.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap Nominatim</a> — address search and geocoding.</li>
</ul>

<p>A condensed version of this list also appears on the map's own attribution strip.</p>

